Visual Bugs:

Gravity Switch Animation for player model rotates around the feet instead of the center of the player for opposites
    -Intended for many rotations, the issue is this happens when rotating 180 degrees as well, aka north->south,
     when it is instead supposed to rotate around the center for these, causing a snap at the end, try it and see)
[MEDIUM PRIORITY] (OLD)

Model is shifted downwards when sneaking
    -Absolute DOWN, seems to do with the player model's placement relative to the hitbox/position
[MEDIUM PRIORITY] (OLD)
    -may also solve: https://github.com/Fusion-Flux/Gravity-Api/issues/63

Walk/Sprint Animations don't play along vertical axis
    -a condition somewhere, intended so you don't wave your arms/legs like you are walking
     when you are jumping/falling, but rotation is not implemented for this correctly.
[MEDIUM PRIORITY] (OLD)
https://github.com/qouteall/GravityChanger/issues/13

